{"input_text": "Question: I would like to calculate the following limit $$\lim_{x \to x_0}{\frac{log\left(\frac{1}{x-x_0}\int_{x_0}^{x}{\frac{\sqrt{f(x)f(x_0)}}{f(u)}du}\right)}{\left(\int_{x_0}^{x}{\frac{1}{f(u)}du}\right)^2}}$$ 
 where $f$ strictly positive and infinitely differentiable. 
 We can define the functions $$h(x)=\int_{x_0}^{x}{\frac{1}{f(u)}du}$$ 
 and  $$h_1(x)=\sqrt{f(x)f(x_0)}h(x)$$ 
 This the limit can be rewritten as  
 $$\lim_{x \to x_0}{\frac{log(\frac{h_1(x)-h_1(x_0)}{x-x_0})}{x-x_0}}\frac{x-x_0}{h_1(x)^2-h_1(x_0)^2}f(x)f(x_0)$$ 
 Finally define $$h_2(x)=log(\frac{h_1(x)-h_1(x_0)}{x-x_0})$$ 
 Thus, 
 $$\lim_{x \to x_0}{\frac{h_2(x)-h_2(x_0)}{x-x_0}}\frac{x-x_0}{h_1(x)^2-h_1(x_0)^2}f(x)f(x_0)$$ 
 where $h_2(x_0)$ is obtained by extending $h_2$ by continuity around $x_0$, which is $0$ 
 I would like to conclude using the derivative slope definition but something is not adding up as I get and undefined behavior.  

Answer: The calculations might be a bit off but the idea should be OK. 
Let $b=-\frac{f^{\prime}(x_{0})}{f(x_{0})}$ and $c=\frac12\frac
{-f^{\prime\prime}(x_{0})f(x_{0})+2(f^{\prime}(x_{0}))^{2}}{(f(x_{0}))^{3}}$
and $d=\frac{1}{2}\left[  \frac{f^{\prime\prime}(x_{0})}{f(x_{0})}-\frac{1}
{2}\frac{(f^{\prime}(x_{0}))^{2}}{(f(x_{0}))^{2}}\right]  $. Use the following
Taylor's formulas
\begin{align*}
f(x)  & =f(x_{0})+f^{\prime}(x_{0})(x-x_{0})+o((x-x_{0})),\\
\frac{1}{f(x)}  & =\frac{1}{f(x_{0})}-\frac{f^{\prime}(x_{0})}{(f(x_{0}))^2
}(x-x_{0})+\frac12\frac{-f^{\prime\prime}(x_{0})f(x_{0})+2(f^{\prime
}(x_{0}))^{2}}{(f(x_{0}))^{3}}(x-x_{0})^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})\\
(f(x))^{1/2}  & =(f(x_{0}))^{1/2}+\frac{1}{2}\frac{f^{\prime}(x_{0})}
{(f(x_{0}))^{1/2}}(x-x_{0})\\
& +\frac{1}{2}\left[  f^{\prime\prime}(x_{0})(f(x_{0}))^{-1/2}-\frac{1}
{2}(f^{\prime}(x_{0}))^{2}(f(x_{0}))^{-3/2}\right]  (x-x_{0})^{2}
+o((x-x_{0})^{2})\\
\log(1+t)  & =t+o(t),
\end{align*}
to write
\begin{align*}
\int_{x_{0}}^{x}\frac{1}{f(u)}\,du  & =\frac{1}{f(x_{0})}\int_{x_{0}}
^{x}\left(  1+b(u-x_{0})+c(u-x_{0})^{2}+o((u-x_{0})^{2})\right)  \,du\\
& =\frac{1}{f(x_{0})}\left(  x-x_{0}+\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})^{2}+\frac{1}
{3}c(x-x_{0})^{3}+o((x-x_{0})^{3})\right)
\end{align*}
and so
$$
\left(  \int_{x_{0}}^{x}\frac{1}{f(u)}\,du\right)  ^{2}=\frac{(x-x_{0})^{2}
}{f^{2}(x_{0})}\left(  1+\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})+o((x-x_{0}))\right)  ^{2}
$$
while
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sqrt{f(x)}}{\sqrt{f(x_{0})}}  & =1+\frac{1}{2}\frac{f^{\prime}(x_{0}
)}{f(x_{0})}(x-x_{0})\\
& +\frac{1}{2}\left[  \frac{f^{\prime\prime}(x_{0})}{f(x_{0})}-\frac{1}
{2}\frac{(f^{\prime}(x_{0}))^{2}}{(f(x_{0}))^{2}}\right]  (x-x_{0}
)^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})
\end{align*}
and so
\begin{align*}
& \log\frac{\sqrt{f(x)f(x_{0})}}{x-x_{0}}\int_{x_{0}}^{x}\frac{1}{f(u)}\,du\\
& =\log\frac{\sqrt{f(x)}}{\sqrt{f(x_{0})}}\left(  1+\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0}
)+\frac{1}{3}c(x-x_{0})^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})\right)  \\
& =\log\left(  1-\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})+d(x-x_{0})^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})\right)
\left(  1+\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})+\frac{1}{3}c(x-x_{0})^{2}+o((x-x_{0}
)^{2})\right)  \\
& =\log\left(  1+d(x-x_{0})^{2}-\frac{1}{4}b^{2}(x-x_{0})^{2}+\frac{1}
{3}c(x-x_{0})^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})\right)  \\
& =\left(  d-\frac{1}{4}b^{2}+\frac{1}{3}c\right)  (x-x_{0})^{2}
+o((x-x_{0})^{2})
\end{align*}
and so you get
\begin{align*}
{\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{x-x_0}\int_{x_0}^{x}{\frac{\sqrt{f(x)f(x_0)}}{f(u)}du}\right)}{\left(\int_{x_0}^{x}{\frac{1}{f(u)}du}\right)^2}}=& \frac{\left(  d-\frac{1}{4}b^{2}+\frac{1}{3}c\right)  (x-x_{0}
)^{2}+o((x-x_{0})^{2})}{\frac{(x-x_{0})^{2}}{f^{2}(x_{0})}\left(  1+\frac
{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})+o((x-x_{0}))\right)  ^{2}}\\
& =\frac{\left(  d-\frac{1}{4}b^{2}+\frac{1}{3}c\right)  +o(1)}{\frac{1}
{f^{2}(x_{0})}\left(  1+\frac{1}{2}b(x-x_{0})+o((x-x_{0}))\right)  ^{2}
}\rightarrow f^{2}(x_{0})\left(  d-\frac{1}{4}b^{2}+\frac{1}{3}c\right)
